  "description": "Advanced Modifications\n\nAdds over 20+ Hullmods with dynamic tooltips and combat effects to expand build possibilities!\n\nDownload\n(Can be added to existing save!)\n\nRequires:\n\nLazyLib\n\nMagicLib\n\nGraphicsLib\n\nThings to expect:\n\n-High-risk high-reward type modifications.\n\n-Mid combat effects to turn the tides!\n\n-Not just stat change, also custom VFX and special effects!.\n\n-Hullmods with special material requirements.\n\nSpoiler\nMaterials used to install hullmods are NOT recovered when uninstalling them,\nThis is intended to force people into thinking twice before making a decision,\nhowever the engine will remember what ship equipped what hullmod (even if destroyed and recovered)\nand you will never have to spend the same materials again to reinstall the same hullmod on that ship.\n\n-Subsystems for upgrading Hullmod effects!\n\nHullmods:\n\nSpoiler\n\nSubsystems:\n\nSpoiler\nSometimes while salvaging a research or a mining station you might be lucky and find a Subsystem!\n\nThese can be installed on ships that already have Advanced Hullmods to unlock their true potential!\n\nEvery hullmod supports full dynamic tooltip, when installing a Subsystem,\nthe tooltip change by listing upgrade effects (if any) and changing all parameters and their colors accordingly\n\nI won't spoil everything here, install the mod and find all possible upgrades yourself!\n\nChangelog:\n\nSpoiler\n-v1.0\nMod release\n\nBalance:\n\nWhile listening to feedback i learnt that aiming toward perfect balance is simply impossible since everyone wants something,\nhence i decided to release this mod as uncompiled source code to give you guys the ability to (change it yourself),\ni codded these hullmods to cascade any change in variables to their dynamic tooltips even if you chain upgrade them with a Subsystem.\n\nCredits:\n\nBig thanks to Spectros and everyone else on the unofficial SS discord whom have provided their feedback\nand helped me balance this mod as much as possible!\n\nAdvanced Modifications is licensed under:\nCreative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International License.",
